# Documentation only: this root overview is not a combined environment to copy.
# Target: independent apps/api product API and AI-owner services/ai HTTP service.
# Writing-required API config: SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (comma-separated exact canonical browser origins).
# SUPABASE_URL requires HTTPS except HTTP loopback (localhost, 127.*, [::1]).
# Origins require HTTPS except local loopback HTTP; no wildcard/path/trailing slash.
# Product bearer auth, active-profile checks, exact CORS and writing CRUD exist.
# SQL migrations/RLS/grants/RPCs enforce ownership, replay and revisions.
# Readiness requires valid writing config and matching api_release_ready RPC true;
# otherwise generic 503. The release RPC also verifies the complete schema catalog.
# Config/readiness need no AI credentials or reachability; later optional feature
# config must not block ordinary saves. Real local writing acceptance is validated.
# Optional until jobs/account operations are enabled: isolated SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY;
# never use this privileged key for normal user queries.
# Optional until protected job invocation is enabled: JOB_TRIGGER_SECRET.
# Optional until AI processing is enabled: AI_SERVICE_URL and AI_SERVICE_TOKEN
# (versioned server credential); validate them only for the enabled AI feature.
# AI service only, later: AI_PROVIDER, AI_API_KEY, AI_MODEL; no provider is selected.
# Never give AI database admin keys or put server/provider credentials in frontends.
# Web uses apps/web/.env.local; mobile uses apps/mobile/.env.local.
# Workspace examples contain current public API origins and bearer configuration.
# apps/api/.env.example now exists with writing-only config; use apps/api/.env.local.
# services/ai implementation/configuration remains reserved for the AI owner.
# Use separate local/deployed environment scopes; see docs/cloud-setup.md for status.
# Complete ownership inventory and migration notes: docs/setup.md.
# Do not put real values, tokens, emails or private content in this overview.
